%% Birgma Governance Portal — Whole-application request sequence
%% A representative end-to-end flow that exercises every architectural layer:
%% an employee signs in, reads an assigned policy, passes its knowledge check,
%% and records a binding acknowledgement. Mirrors the prose lifecycle in
%% ARCHITECTURE-AND-DECISIONS.md §3 and HLD.md.
%%
%% HOW TO OPEN IN LUCIDCHART: File → Import Diagram → Mermaid (paste this file).
%% Also renders on github.com, mermaid.live, VS Code, and request-sequence.html.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Employee (browser SPA)
    participant N as nginx (web, TLS/CSP/proxy)
    participant E as Microsoft Entra ID
    participant A as API (Express 5)
    participant G as Microsoft Graph / SharePoint
    participant D as PostgreSQL 16

    Note over U,E: One-time interactive sign-in (MSAL PKCE)
    U->>E: authorize (PKCE)
    E-->>U: id/access token (roles, scope)

    Note over U,D: Every API call is same-origin, Bearer-token, per-request authorized
    U->>N: GET /api/policies (Bearer)
    N->>A: proxy /api → :8080
    A->>E: validate JWT (JWKS, iss/aud/tid/scope, delegated-only)
    E-->>A: JWKS (cached)
    A->>D: effective-membership + publish-gate query
    D-->>A: assigned, published policies
    A-->>U: policy list (private-by-default)

    U->>N: GET /api/policies/:id/content
    N->>A: proxy
    A->>A: canRead (role ∪ owner ∪ approver ∪ published)
    A->>G: Sites.Selected fetch (Office→PDF if needed)
    G-->>A: document stream
    A-->>U: inline PDF (blob, CSP frame-src)

    Note over U,D: Knowledge-check gate — graded server-side, never trusted from client
    U->>N: POST /api/policies/:id/quiz/attempt (answers)
    N->>A: proxy
    A->>D: advisory lock, insert quiz_attempts (append-only)
    D-->>A: score + passed=true
    A-->>U: result (pass)

    Note over U,D: Binding acknowledgement — append-only, identity+version stamped
    U->>N: POST /api/signatures (policyId, fullName)
    N->>A: proxy
    A->>A: quiz-gate check + canRead
    A->>D: insert signatures (UPDATE/DELETE revoked at grant layer)
    A->>D: insert audit_log (best-effort, non-blocking)
    D-->>A: committed
    A-->>U: acknowledgement recorded
